        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[About Certifications]]></title>
            <link>https://dudukling.github.io/my-blog/blog/about-certifications</link>
            <guid>https://dudukling.github.io/my-blog/blog/about-certifications</guid>
            <pubDate>Tue, 27 Feb 2024 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[Just a few thoughts on certifications:]]></description>
            <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Just a few thoughts on certifications:</p>
<p>Certifications are a very controversial topic, but I really couldn't care less.</p>
<p>I see certifications as a way to continually acquiring new knowledge and applying it everywhere.</p>
<p>A professional's competences are mix of knowledge, skill, and attitude.</p>
<p>What I see as a good professional, is someone who continually invests in their self-development, acquires new knowledge, applies their knowledge by delivering to the environment they are working in, and, most importantly, invests in their soft skills.</p>]]></content:encoded>
            <category>aws</category>
            <category>psm</category>
            <category>devops</category>
            <category>certification</category>
        </item>
